{
  "dom_id": "step-q6277",
  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "Solve the inequality $-2y>18.$",
  "worked_solution": "The variable $y$ is being *multiplied* by $-2.$ To isolate $y,$ we perform the *opposite* operation, which is *dividing* by $-2.$ Remember to perform the same operation on both sides.\n\nAlso, when multiplying or dividing an inequality by a negative number, we need to flip the inequality sign:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2y\\,\\, & >\\,\\,18 \\\\ \\frac{-2y}{-2}\\,\\, & <\\,\\,\\frac{18}{-2} \\\\ \\frac{-2y}{-2}\\,\\, & <\\,\\,-9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can cancel a common factor of $-2$ from both the numerator and denominator.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-2y}{-2} & <-9 \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{-2}y}{\\cancel{-2}} & <-9 \\\\ y & <-9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $y<-9.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
